course: dictionary
lesson: 8703
title: The smallest step
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A semitone is the smallest step between two notes in Western music. On a piano, it is the move to the very next key, black or white. «A sharp raises a note by a semitone, the smallest step on a piano.» So a sharp moves the note one key higher.
explain: A semitone is half a tone, and two semitones make one whole tone. From C to C sharp is one semitone. From C to D is a whole tone, which is two semitones, because it passes C sharp on the way.
explain: «A flat, which looks like a small b, lowers it by a semitone.» Sharps go up and flats go down, each by one semitone. An octave, from one C to the next C, has 12 semitones, so counting semitones is like counting along a number line, one step at a time.
fact: A semitone is the smallest step between two notes in Western music.
fact: Two semitones make one whole tone, so a semitone is half a tone.
fact: On a piano, a semitone is the step to the very next key, black or white.
fact: A sharp raises a note by a semitone, and a flat lowers it by a semitone.
fact: An octave has 12 semitones.
exercise: On a piano, what is one semitone? | The whole keyboard | The length of one bar of music | A jump over three keys | *The step to the very next key, black or white
exercise: «A sharp raises a note by a semitone.» What does a sharp do to a note? | Raises it by a whole octave | Lowers it by one semitone | *Raises it by one semitone | Makes it last longer
exercise: How many semitones make one whole tone? | *2 | 8 | 12 | 1
test: How many semitones are in an octave? | 24 | 6 | 8 | *12
test: «A flat, which looks like a small b, lowers it by a semitone.» What does a flat do to a note? | Raises it by a whole tone | Makes it louder | *Lowers it by one semitone | Moves it up an octave
exam: Which pair of notes is only one semitone apart? | G and C | *E and F | C and E | C and D
